      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a really strong start... i love the phrasing \"mastermind who convinced them to become the instruments of his own political destinies.\" \n\nit feels like you're suggesting that the economic stuff was almost just a backdrop or a tool he used, rather than the actual cause. can you expand on that? specifically, can you write a section that frames the bread riots and the famines as things that were only politically significant because he knew how to weaponize them for his own agenda?",
