    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's intense. it's almost like you're portraying him as a sort of dark architect of the chaos. \n\nto really nail the \"great man\" angle for my book, i want to lean even harder into the idea that the social forces were essentially irrelevant without him. how would you frame it if we argued that even if the famine hadn't happened, he still would have found a way to engineer a similar political crisis to achieve his goals? basically, that his willpower was more powerful than historical material conditions?",
